class:: MIRaColormap
summary:: Perceptually uniform color lookup tables for MIR visual displays
categories:: GUI>Color, Libraries>MIR
related:: Classes/MIRaPlot, Classes/MIRaGUI, Guides/MIRa-file-visualization

description::
MIRaColormap provides perceptually uniform color lookup tables and packed 32-bit ARGB pixel buffers for high-performance raster rendering of time-frequency representations (such as spectrograms and chromagrams) in SuperCollider.

It includes 5 standard color palettes widely used in music information retrieval and data visualization toolkits (such as matplotlib and librosa):
list::
## strong::\magma::: Dark violet through crimson and bright orange to golden yellow. Ideal for high-contrast time-frequency spectrograms.
## strong::\viridis::: Deep navy blue through emerald green to bright warm yellow. Perceptually linear across lightness and colorblind-safe.
## strong::\plasma::: Dark indigo purple through magenta and vibrant pink to yellow. High perceptual dynamic range.
## strong::\inferno::: Black through intense violet and fiery orange to light yellow. Accentuates quiet background noise floors and peaks.
## strong::\coolwarm::: Symmetrical diverging blue-to-red colormap centered at neutral gray. Ideal for bipolar features and correlation matrices.
::

classmethods::

method:: colorAt
Returns an interpolated link::Classes/Color:: for a normalized scalar value between 0.0 and 1.0.
argument:: val
Normalized float value code::[0.0, 1.0]::.
argument:: name
Symbol naming the colormap (e.g. code::\magma::, code::\viridis::).
returns:: A link::Classes/Color::.

method:: pixelAt
Returns a 32-bit packed integer in ARGB format code::(0xAARRGGBB):: for fast direct blitting into link::Classes/Image:: pixel buffers.
argument:: val
Normalized float value code::[0.0, 1.0]::.
argument:: name
Colormap symbol.
returns:: An link::Classes/Integer::.

method:: table
Returns an link::Classes/Array:: of 256 pre-calculated link::Classes/Color:: instances for the requested palette.
argument:: name
Colormap symbol.
argument:: size
Number of color steps (default: 256).
returns:: An link::Classes/Array:: of link::Classes/Color::.

method:: pixelTable
Returns an link::Classes/Int32Array:: of 256 pre-computed packed 32-bit ARGB color pixels.
argument:: name
Colormap symbol.
argument:: size
Table size (default: 256).
returns:: An link::Classes/Int32Array::.

method:: drawColorbar
Renders a colorbar gradient inside a specified rectangle using link::Classes/Pen::.
argument:: rect
A link::Classes/Rect::.
argument:: name
Colormap symbol (e.g. code::\magma::).
argument:: vertical
Boolean indicating vertical (true) or horizontal (false) gradient orientation.

examples::
code::
(
// Preview all 5 standard MIRa colormaps:
var win = Window("MIRa Colormap Palettes", Rect(100, 100, 520, 260)).front;
var names = [\magma, \viridis, \plasma, \inferno, \coolwarm];
win.view.background = Color(0.12, 0.12, 0.14);

win.drawFunc = {
    names.do { |name, i|
        var y = 20 + (i * 45);
        Pen.fillColor = Color.white;
        Pen.font = Font("Sans", 11, true);
        Pen.stringAtPoint(name.asString.capitalize, Point(20, y + 4));
        MIRaColormap.drawColorbar(Rect(110, y, 380, 24), name, vertical: false);
    };
};
win.refresh;
)
::
